                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d7356d6-0ff4-3771-b504-ba0fc855a369",
                        "entry_id": "b06df842-5a53-3b34-9484-bae01c031631",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A member of the Exclusive Brethren."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9caf502-b525-465c-8cad-39e859ca91c1",
                                "sense_id": "9d7356d6-0ff4-3771-b504-ba0fc855a369",
                                "text": "The Darbyite quietly assumes that Christ is not ashamed to call his party brethren, and that He would be thoroughly ashamed to apply the name to any one else."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "798c9dee-651d-4c3c-9236-396e1737033e",
                                "sense_id": "9d7356d6-0ff4-3771-b504-ba0fc855a369",
                                "text": "The \"sad step,\" Mr. Howard states, was that of belonging to a \"gathering\" at Peckham, whose members had all been turned out from the fold of the Brethren by the act of a small clique of leading Darbyites."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5ebfe6e-48cb-42ac-bd86-2b0ed9af524d",
                                "sense_id": "9d7356d6-0ff4-3771-b504-ba0fc855a369",
                                "text": "The Darbyites argued against the war on national, cultural, grounds and the Cobdenites on international and civilizational."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
